[623.003489, "o", "Help on class LinearGaussianMLE in module pgmpy.parameter_estimator.linear_gaussian_mle:\r\n\r\nclass L\bLi\bin\bne\bea\bar\brG\bGa\bau\bus\bss\bsi\bia\ban\bnM\bML\bLE\bE(pgmpy.parameter_estimator.base.GaussianParameterEstimator)\r\n |  LinearGaussianMLE(std_estimator: 'str' = 'unbiased') -> 'None'\r\n |\r\n |  Computes parameters for a LinearGaussianBayesianNetwork using Maximum Likelihood Estimation.\r\n |\r\n |  For root nodes, the mean and variance are estimated directly from data. For non-root\r\n"]
[623.003716, "o", " |  nodes, a linear regression is fit to estimate the regression coefficients and intercept;\r\n |  the residual standard deviation is used as the noise parameter.\r\n |\r\n |  Parameters\r\n |  ----------\r\n |  std_estimator: {\"unbiased\", \"mle\"}, default=\"unbiased\"\r\n |      Method used to estimate the noise standard deviation.\r\n |      - ``\"unbiased\"``: uses ``ddof = 1`` for root nodes and ``ddof = 1 + n_parents``\r\n |        for non-root nodes.\r\n |      - ``\"mle\"``: uses ``ddof = 0`` (biased, maximum likelihood estimate).\r\n |\r\n |  Attributes\r\n |  ----------\r\n |  parameters_ : list of LinearGaussianCPD\r\n"]
[623.003905, "o", " |      Learned Gaussian conditional probability distributions, one per\r\n |      variable in the model, ordered by `self._model.nodes()`. Populated by\r\n |      `fit`.\r\n |\r\n |  Examples\r\n |  --------\r\n |  >>> import numpy as np\r\n |  >>> import pandas as pd\r\n |  >>> from pgmpy.models import LinearGaussianBayesianNetwork\r\n |  >>> from pgmpy.parameter_estimator import LinearGaussianMLE\r\n"]
[623.004028, "o", " |  >>> rng = np.random.default_rng(42)\r\n |  >>> data = pd.DataFrame(rng.normal(0, 1, (100, 3)), columns=[\"x1\", \"x2\", \"x3\"])\r\n |  >>> model = LinearGaussianBayesianNetwork([(\"x1\", \"x2\"), (\"x2\", \"x3\")])\r\n |  >>> estimator = LinearGaussianMLE()\r\n"]
[623.004558, "o", " |  >>> estimator.fit(model, data).parameters_  # doctest: +ELLIPSIS +NORMALIZE_WHITESPACE\r\n |  [<LinearGaussianCPD: P(x1) = N(...) at 0x...>,\r\n |   <LinearGaussianCPD: P(x2 | x1) = N(...) at 0x...>,\r\n\u001b[7m--More--\u001b[27m"]
[627.122223, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > full_pipeline.py\nimport pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\nfrom pgmpy.models import LinearGaussianBayesianNetwork\nfrom pgmpy.sampling import BayesianModelSampling\nfrom pgmpy.factors.continuous import LinearGaussianCPD\n\ndf = pd.read_csv('/app/bn_sample_10k.csv')\n\ncorrected_edges = [\n    ('M', 'U'),\n    ('Y', 'U'),\n    ('D', 'U'),\n    ('D', 'Y'),\n    ('R', 'U'),\n    ('M', 'R')\n]\n\n# 2) Learn Bayesian Network\nmodel = LinearGaussianBayesianNetwork(corrected_edges)\nmodel.fit(df)\nprint(\"Fitted model nodes/edges:\", model.nodes(), model.edges())\n\n# 3) Perform causal intervention on Y, setting its value to 0.0 (variance 1e-9)\nintervened_edges = [e for e in corrected_edges if e[0] != 'Y']\nprint(\"Intervened edges:\", intervened_edges)\n\n# Save intervened_dag.csv\ndf_intervened = pd.DataFrame(intervened_edges, columns=['to', 'from'])\ndf_intervened.to_csv('/app/intervened_dag.csv', index=False)\nprint(\"Saved /app/intervened_dag.csv\")\n\n# Create intervened model and fit\nintervened_model = LinearGaussianBayesianNetwork(intervened_edges)\nintervened_model.fit(df)\n\n# Override CPD of Y to be deterministic / zero variance around 0.0\ncpd_y = LinearGaussianCPD('Y', beta=[0.0], variance=1e-9)\nintervened_model.add_cpds(cpd_y)\n\nprint(\"Intervened model check:\", intervened_model.check_model())\n\n# 5) Sample 10k points\nsampler = BayesianModelSampling(intervened_model)\nsamples = sampler.forward_sample(size=10000)\nsamples = samples[df.columns]\nsamples.to_csv('/app/final_bn_sample.csv', index=False)\nprint(\"Saved /app/final_bn_sample.csv with shape:\", samples.shape)\nprint(samples.head())\n\nEOF\n./venv/bin/python full_pipeline.py\n"]
[627.122475, "o", "\u0007\r\r\u001b[K\r\n...skipping 39 lines\r\n"]
