[660.268785, "o", "Help on class LinearGaussianCPD in module pgmpy.factors.continuous.LinearGaussianCPD:\r\n\r\nclass L\bLi\bin\bne\bea\bar\brG\bGa\bau\bus\bss\bsi\bia\ban\bnC\bCP\bPD\bD(pgmpy.factors.base.BaseFactor)\r\n |  LinearGaussianCPD(variable, beta, std, evidence=[])\r\n |\r\n |  Defines a Linear Gaussian CPD.\r\n |\r\n"]
[660.269081, "o", " |  The Linear Gaussian CPD makes the following assumptions [1]:\r\n |      1) The variable is Gaussian/Normally distributed.\r\n |      2) The mean of the variable depends on the values of the parents and the\r\n |          intercept term.\r\n |      3) The variance is independent of other variables.\r\n |\r\n |  For example,\r\n |\r\n"]
[660.269202, "o", " |  .. math::\r\n |\r\n |    p(Y|X) = N(0.9 - 2x; 1)\r\n |\r\n |  Here, :math:`0.9 - 2x` is the mean of the variable :math:`Y` and the\r\n |  standard deviation is 1.\r\n |\r\n |  In generalized terms, let :math:`Y` be a Gaussian variable with parents\r\n |  :math:`X_1, X_2, \\cdots, X_k`. Assuming linear relationship between Y and\r\n |  \\mathbf{X}, the conditional distribution of Y can be defined as:\r\n |\r\n |  .. math:: p(Y |x1, x2, ..., xk) = \\mathcal{N}(\\beta_0 + x1*\\beta_1 + ......... + xk*\\beta_k ; \\sigma)\r\n |\r\n"]
[660.269474, "o", " |  References\r\n |  ----------\r\n |  .. [1] https://cedar.buffalo.edu/~srihari/CSE574/Chap8/Ch8-PGM-GaussianBNs/8.5%20GaussianBNs.pdf\r\n |\r\n |  Parameters\r\n |  ----------\r\n |\r\n |  variable: any hashable python object\r\n |      The variable whose CPD is defined.\r\n |\r\n |  beta: list (array-like)\r\n\u001b[7m--More--\u001b[27m"]
[673.726913, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > full_pipeline.py\nimport pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\nfrom pgmpy.models import LinearGaussianBayesianNetwork\nfrom pgmpy.sampling import BayesianModelSampling\nfrom pgmpy.factors.continuous import LinearGaussianCPD\n\ndf = pd.read_csv('/app/bn_sample_10k.csv')\n\ncorrected_edges = [\n    ('M', 'U'),\n    ('Y', 'U'),\n    ('D', 'U'),\n    ('D', 'Y'),\n    ('R', 'U'),\n    ('M', 'R')\n]\n\n# 2) Learn Bayesian Network\nmodel = LinearGaussianBayesianNetwork(corrected_edges)\nmodel.fit(df)\nprint(\"Fitted model nodes/edges:\", model.nodes(), model.edges())\n\n# 3) Perform causal intervention on Y, setting its value to 0.0 (variance 10e-9)\nintervened_edges = [e for e in corrected_edges if e[0] != 'Y']\nprint(\n\n# Save intervened_dag.csv\ndf_intervened = pd.DataFrame(intervened_edges, columns=['to', 'from'])\ndf_intervened.to_csv('/app/intervened_dag.csv', index=False)\nprint(\"Saved /app/intervened_dag.csv\")\n\n# Create intervened model and fit\nintervened_model = LinearGaussianBayesianNetwork(intervened_edges)\nintervened_model.fit(df)\n\n# Override CPD of Y to be deterministic / zero variance around 0.0 (std = sqrt(10e-9))\ncpd_y = LinearGaussianCPD('Y', beta=[0.0], std=np.sqrt(10e-9), evidence=[])\nintervened_model.add_cpds(cpd_y)\n\nprint(\"Intervened model check:\", intervened_model.check_model())\n\n# 5) Sample 10k points\nsampler = BayesianModelSampling(intervened_model)\nsamples = sampler.forward_sample(size=10000)\nsamples = samples[df.columns]\nsamples.to_csv('/app/final_bn_sample.csv', index=False)\nprint(\"Saved /app/final_bn_sample.csv with shape:\", samples.shape)\nprint(samples.head())\nEOF\n./venv/bin/python full_pipeline.py\n"]
[673.727202, "o", "\u0007\r\r\u001b[K\r\n...skipping 39 lines\r\n"]
[673.727506, "o", "\r |      other: LinearGaussianCPD instance\r\n |          The other LinearGaussianCPD object to compare with.\r\n |\r\n |      Returns\r\n"]
[673.727579, "o", " |      -------\r\n |      bool\r\n |          True if the two LinearGaussianCPD objects are equal, False otherwise.\r\n |\r\n"]
[673.727807, "o", " |  _\b__\b_i\bin\bni\bit\bt_\b__\b_(self, variable, beta, std, evidence=[])\r\n |      Initialize self.  See help(type(self)) for accurate signature.\r\n |\r\n |  _\b__\b_r\bre\bep\bpr\br_\b__\b_(self)\r\n |      Return repr(self).\r\n |\r\n |  _\b__\b_s\bst\btr\br_\b__\b_(self)\r\n |      Return str(self).\r\n |\r\n |  c\bco\bop\bpy\by(self)\r\n |      Returns a copy of the distribution.\r\n |\r\n |      Returns\r\n"]
