[837.135213, "o", " |      node: string, int or any hashable python object.\r\n |          The node whose children would be returned.\r\n |\r\n |      Examples\r\n |      --------\r\n |      >>> from pgmpy.base import DAG\r\n |      >>> g = DAG(\r\n |      ...     ebunch=[\r\n |      ...         (\"A\", \"B\"),\r\n |      ...         (\"C\", \"B\"),\r\n |      ...         (\"B\", \"D\"),\r\n |      ...         (\"B\", \"E\"),\r\n |      ...         (\"B\", \"F\"),\r\n |      ...         (\"E\", \"G\"),\r\n |      ...     ]\r\n |      ... )\r\n |      >>> g.get_children(node=\"B\")\r\n |      ['D', 'E', 'F']\r\n |\r\n |  g\bge\bet\bt_\b_i\bim\bmm\bmo\bor\bra\bal\bli\bit\bti\bie\bes\bs(self) -> 'dict[Hashable, list[tuple[Hashable, Hashable]]]'\r\n |      Finds all the immoralities in the model\r\n |      A v-structure X -> Z <- Y is an immorality if there is no direct edge between X and Y .\r\n |\r\n |      Returns\r\n |      -------\r\n"]
