[895.297274, "o", " |          A view of edge attributes, usually it iterates over (u, v)\r\n |          or (u, v, d) tuples of edges, but can also be used for\r\n |          attribute lookup as `edges[u, v]['foo']`.\r\n |\r\n |      Examples\r\n |      --------\r\n |      >>> G = nx.DiGraph()\r\n |      >>> G.add_edge(1, 2, color=\"blue\")\r\n |      >>> G.in_edges()\r\n |      InEdgeView([(1, 2)])\r\n |      >>> G.in_edges(nbunch=2)\r\n |      InEdgeDataView([(1, 2)])\r\n |\r\n |      See Also\r\n |      --------\r\n |      edges\r\n |\r\n"]
